  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V2X Systems has $1.2B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date, across 615 awards with an average award size of $2M. Obligations are down 27.7% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, accounting for $1B of obligations in the current fiscal year. Facilities Support Services is the company’s largest NAICS market with $920M in obligations, followed by All Other Legal Services at $158M. Historical fiscal-year obligations show variability: FY21 $1.4B, FY22 $1.1B, FY23 $2B, FY24 $1.6B, FY25 $1.7B, and FY26 $1.2B. The Department of Justice and the Department of State are the next largest buying agencies at $158M and $42.2M respectively. Smaller agency customers in FY2026 to date include the Department of Health and Human Services at $1.5M and the Department of Homeland Security at $377K. The company’s work spans services and equipment markets with measurable concentration in facilities support and legal services, and smaller positions in communications repair, engineering, and telecommunications categories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are V2X Systems’ biggest federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $158M and the Department of State obligated $42.2M. The Department of Health and Human Services and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $1.5M and $377K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are V2X Systems’ primary contract markets?",
        "body": "Facilities Support Services is the largest market at $920M in FY2026 to date. All Other Legal Services is the second-largest market at $158M, followed by Communication Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $42.1M and Engineering Services at $41.5M. Smaller markets include All Other Telecommunications at $17.3M and Other Warehousing and Storage at $1.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
